      <guid>//localhost:1313/docs/04-advanced-ui-components/uimenu-and-image-pickers/6.8.-wrapping-up-a-bit-of-polishing/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;68-wrapping-up-a-bit-of-polishing&#34;&gt;6.8. Wrapping Up: a bit of polishing&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#68-wrapping-up-a-bit-of-polishing&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We will polish the TableView a little bit to make our TableView look like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;//localhost:1313/gitbook-assets/Screenshot%202023-05-20%20at%205.18.17%20PM%20%282%29.png&#34; alt=&#34;&#34; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Let&amp;rsquo;s make the following changes to the code:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Removing the separator line:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Open ViewController.swift file. Put the following line in &lt;code&gt;viewDidLoad()&lt;/code&gt; method:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre class=&#34;language-swift&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;lang-swift&#34;&gt;override func viewDidLoad() {&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;    super.viewDidLoad()&#xA;&lt;/strong&gt;    title = &#34;Expense App&#34;&#xA;    &#xA;    //MARK: manipulating TableView separator line...&#xA;    firstScreen.tableViewExpense.separatorStyle = .none&#xA;    &#xA;    //Codes omitted...&#xA;}&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working with shadows:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Open the TableViewExpenseCell.swift file. Update the code in the method where we initialize the &lt;code&gt;wrapperCellView&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;setupWrapperCellView()&lt;/code&gt;) :&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
